Code-Layout, Readability and Reusability
1. Development Structure

The project is organized into separate components for user management, role management, table creation, and ACL configuration.

2. Organized Access Control

Separate ACL configurations are maintained for READ, CREATE, WRITE, and DELETE operations.

3. Readability

The access-control logic is structured clearly so that team members can understand and maintain the configuration.

4. Reusability

The ACL-based approach can be extended to other tables, branches, roles, and access requirements.

5. Maintainability

The project structure allows future modifications to access rules without affecting unrelated components.
